    {
      "id": 198744,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-06-22T14:02:38.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"much0gust0\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n much0gust0:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Haha, it truly shows how special this &nbsp;company is that people would want to randomly stop by a stranger's workplace. I love everything about this.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You're not wrong. OTH, other workplaces I've visited for which I didn't know anyone working there are below. Most of these are tours, but then if GtG offered tours of their warehouse, I bet people would take them.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul><li>Radiology center at IUPUI. We got a tour of the imaging machines and 3D printing. This was 10+ years ago when 3D printing was much more rare.</li><li>Tortilla factory in Cabo San Lucas. Part of a food tour.</li><li>Many vineyards and a few breweries</li><li>Candy factory in Talinn. Part of a tour.</li><li>Coffee plantation tour.</li><li>Bacardi Distillery tour.</li></ul>\n&nbsp;\n<p>Ugh. Remembering and listing all the tours is getting tedious, but I expect you get the point.</p>",
